PythonScriptRunner — AppImage Build Instructions
=================================================

OVERVIEW
--------
The AppImage bundles a self-contained Python 3.12 interpreter (no system Python
required) along with the app source and the Tcl/Tk shared libraries needed for
the tkinter GUI. On first launch it seeds ~/.local/share/PythonScriptRunner/
with the default scripts; on every subsequent launch it syncs the app code from
the AppImage so updates are always picked up automatically.


BUILD PREREQUISITES (Linux x86_64 only)
----------------------------------------
  sudo apt install curl tar tcl8.6 tk8.6        # Debian / Ubuntu
  sudo dnf install curl tar tcl tk              # Fedora / RHEL / CentOS
  sudo pacman -S curl tar tcl tk                # Arch


BUILD STEPS
-----------
1. Transfer the project to a Linux x86_64 machine (or VM / container).

2. From the project root, run the build script:

     cd build
     bash build-appimage.sh

3. The script will:
   a. Download python-build-standalone (CPython 3.12, ~30 MB, cached after first run)
   b. Copy libtcl8.6 / libtk8.6 from the build machine into the AppDir
   c. Copy the app source (PythonScriptRunner.py, runner/, scripts/)
   d. Download appimagetool (cached after first run)
   e. Package everything into:  PythonScriptRunner-x86_64.AppImage

4. Output file location:
     <project-root>/PythonScriptRunner-x86_64.AppImage


RUNNING THE APPIMAGE
--------------------
  chmod +x PythonScriptRunner-x86_64.AppImage
  ./PythonScriptRunner-x86_64.AppImage

The only runtime requirement on target machines is FUSE.
  - Modern Linux (kernel 5.13+): FUSE is built in — nothing to install.
  - Older systems:  sudo apt install fuse   OR   sudo dnf install fuse


USER DATA LOCATION
------------------
All writable data lives outside the AppImage in:
  ~/.local/share/PythonScriptRunner/

  scripts/          User scripts and manifests (seeded on first run, never overwritten)
  requirements.txt  Dependencies for user scripts (seeded on first run)
  .venv/            Auto-created virtual environment for running user scripts
  logs/             Script output logs (if logging is enabled in a manifest)

The app code (PythonScriptRunner.py, runner/) is synced from the AppImage on
every launch, so distributing a new AppImage automatically updates the code
while leaving the user's scripts and venv untouched.


ADDING AN ICON
--------------
Place a 256x256 PNG named icon.png in the project root before building.
If no icon.png is found, the build script generates a solid blue placeholder.


UPDATING PYTHON VERSION
-----------------------
Edit the top of build/build-appimage.sh and change:
  PYTHON_VERSION="3.12.9"
  PYTHON_RELEASE="20250317"

Releases are listed at:
  https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases


BUILD ARTEFACTS (git-ignored)
------------------------------
The following are excluded from version control via .gitignore:
  *.AppImage
  build/AppDir/
  build/python-standalone.tar.gz
  build/appimagetool-*.AppImage


FILES IN build/
---------------
  build-appimage.sh          Main build script
  AppRun                     AppImage entry point (launcher)
  PythonScriptRunner.desktop Desktop entry required by AppImage spec
  instructions               This file
